  "ownership_scope": "The product language benchmark is physically owned by leserpent-vm and directly imports leserpent_hir and leserpent_vm. The legacy native facade no longer declares or contains it. The existing gewyvern_validate benchmark entry selects the memory product target without SQLite. Library APIs, versions, report schema and performance budgets are unchanged.",
  "export_scope": "The closed language example inventory now admits only native_counter.rs. The exporter succeeds without a product example directory and refuses product files reintroduced into the language directory. Closed VM manifest projection rejects new explicit example sections instead of silently dropping a product target. The complete verified native source checkpoint has the same manifest hash and all 312 file contents as the previous queued-example checkpoint.",
  "verification_scope": "Two workload tests pass with both default and disabled-default product features. The lean benchmark emits the original 64-effect report; normal/build dependencies exclude both language facades and SQLite. Four existing benchmark-validator tests, exporter tests, strict lint and full isolated export pass locally. CI source was parsed and the new product example test target checked, not run on a remote CI service. Historical proofs retain their checkpoint paths/hashes.",
  "remaining_boundaries": [
    "Complete declared-language/reference compatibility acceptance.",
    "Production host-neutral durable recovery and real GUI/FFI integration.",
    "Registry publication and physical repository extraction."
  ],
